# Platform-Portable Helpers (esnacc)

CI builds on **Ubuntu** as well as Windows. Do **not** call MSVC-only CRT APIs (`strcpy_s`, `strcat_s`, `fopen_s`, `_MAX_PATH`, …) directly in new or edited compiler/c-lib code without going through the existing portability layer.

## Required includes

| Need | Include | Notes |
|------|---------|-------|
| Safe string/file macros on Linux | `c-lib/include/asn-config.h` | Maps `strcpy_s`, `strcat_s`, `sprintf_s`, `fopen_s`, `_MAX_PATH`, `_mkdir`, … on non-`_WIN32` |
| Portable `fopen` wrapper | `c-lib/include/platform-functions.h` | `myfopen`, `mytolower` (also pulled in via `asn-config.h` on Linux) |
| ASN.1 date ↔ unix time | `compiler/core/time_helpers.h` | `ConvertDateToUnixTime`, `ConvertUnixTimeToISO`, `ConvertUnixTimeToNumericDate`, … |
| Paths, directories, file cache | `compiler/core/cpp_c_helper.h` | `getDirectoryWithDelimiterFromPath`, `createDirectories`, `findFiles`, `writeFile`, … |
| C++ path/file utilities | `compiler/core/cpp_helper.h` | C++ helpers used from `.cpp` back-ends |

**Pattern:** mirror `compiler/core/time_helpers.c` and `compiler/core/snacc-validation-rules.cpp` — include `asn-config.h` from `c-lib/include/` in any new `.c` / `.cpp` under `compiler/` that uses `_s` string functions or `_MAX_PATH`.

## Rules

1. **Never** add raw `fopen` / `strcpy` / `strcat` shims in a single file — extend or use `asn-config.h` / `platform-functions.c` instead.
2. **Never** assume `_WIN32` for compiler core logic; Windows-only code belongs behind `#ifdef _WIN32` with a portable default.
3. After editing portable code, verify **CMake Release build** (and `ctest` when tests exist) — local MSVC success alone is not enough.
4. When adding file I/O in the compiler core, prefer **`myfopen`** (via `fopen_s` macro) over direct `fopen`.
5. **Unit tests** that compile compiler `.c` sources directly (not via the `compiler` target) must also link **`c-lib`** (or at least `c-lib/src/platform-functions.c`) when those sources use `fopen_s` / `asn-config.h` on Linux.

## Agent checklist

Before finishing a compiler/c-lib change that touches strings, paths, or files:

- [ ] Includes `asn-config.h` if using `*_s` CRT helpers or `_MAX_PATH`
- [ ] Uses `time_helpers.h` for date parsing/formatting (not ad-hoc `strftime`/`sscanf`)
- [ ] Uses `cpp_c_helper.h` / `cpp_helper.h` for directory creation and path normalization when applicable
